# Implementation notes

Grafana Tempo supports local filesystem storage for single-node development and documents OTLP receiver configuration on ports 4317/4318. The 24h retention here is intentionally a development default, not a production sizing recommendation. citeturn892261search1turn892261search0

Tempo 3.0 supports monolithic `-target=all`; this patch keeps that simple model and does not introduce object storage or distributed deployment. citeturn892261search2

Alerting remains Prometheus -> Alertmanager. Application code does not decide notification routing.

The API has no `depends_on: tempo`, so Tempo can be stopped after the API starts. Trace export failures are logged and dropped by the batch exporter rather than returned as API startup failures.

# Phase 4/5 — Sprint 21/22 Tasks

## Sprint 21 — Tempo

### 9.11 Tempo integration
- Configure OpenTelemetry OTLP/HTTP from the API to Tempo.
- Keep Tempo out of API startup dependencies.
- Fail open when exporter initialization fails.
- Log asynchronous export failures without terminating the API.
- Extract W3C trace context and create server spans.
- Provision Tempo in Grafana.
- Smoke-test traces end-to-end.

### 9.12 Trace retention/storage
- Use Tempo monolithic/local storage for development.
- Persist WAL and trace blocks in `tempo-data`.
- Set trace block retention to 24h.
- Set compacted-block retention to 1h.
- Initialize the shared volume as UID/GID 10001 to prevent permissions failures.
- Treat 2 GiB as the development storage target; monitor disk usage rather than adding distributed storage in this milestone.

## Sprint 22 — Alertmanager

### 9.13 Alerting architecture
- Prometheus evaluates alert rules.
- Prometheus forwards firing alerts to Alertmanager.
- Alertmanager owns grouping, repeat intervals, and inhibition.
- Keep alerting logic out of application code.
- Leave notification integration as an operator-owned receiver configuration.

### 9.14 Initial production alerts
- API unavailable.
- API 5xx ratio > 5%.
- External upstream 5xx ratio > 10%.
- Any external retry exhaustion in the last 10 minutes.
- Elevated worker failure rate.
- Sustained external rate-limit pressure.
- Cache hit ratio < 70% under meaningful traffic.
- Database pool has zero connections.
- Validate rule syntax with `promtool check rules`.
- Validate Prometheus -> Alertmanager connectivity.
